From: Cursor Agent <cursoragent@cursor.com>
Date: Fri, 6 Nov 2026 01:55:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Keep library documents internal by default, and gate the
 affiliate library behind one audited checkbox.

The document library could only say "published" or "not published", so an
internal strategy document had no safe home. Now every document carries a
visibility, and there are exactly two values:

  internal   admin only. Never returned by an affiliate query, never served
             from a public path. This is the default for a new PDF.
  affiliate  an admin ticked "Affiliate library". A SIGNED-IN affiliate sees it
             in the portal's Printed Materials through a signed storage URL.
             Still not public: no third value, no public query, no public URL.

Server-enforced, not just a hidden button:
  - affiliateResources.publishedLiterature now requires visibility='affiliate'
    AND isPublished=1, then re-checks both in memory with the same shared
    predicate the admin page uses.
  - affiliateLiterature.adminUpload/adminUpdate are adminProcedure, and
    inAffiliateLibrary is the ONLY field that writes visibility. A plain
    isPublished input would let a stale client publish without touching
    visibility, so it is gone.
  - The toggle writes visibility, isPublished, affiliateToggledAt,
    affiliateToggledBy and affiliateToggledByName in one row update, so the
    three can never disagree.
  - fileKey now sits under library-documents/, which server/storage.ts puts in
    the private Supabase bucket and server/_core/storageProxy.ts refuses on the
    public proxy. An internal document has no public address even if the key
    leaks.
  - affiliateResources.adminSignedFile is an adminProcedure, for the admin
    page's Open button. Affiliates cannot reach it.

The new docs/sql/0250_library_internal_documents.tidb.sql is copied verbatim
from the frontend repo, where it is the single source for the TiDB paste.

Apply from the cabinet-backend repository root:

    git apply /path/to/cabinet-backend-library-internal-documents.patch

Then, in this order:
  1. Paste docs/sql/0250_library_internal_documents.tidb.sql in the TiDB editor.
  2. Deploy this patch (the schema selects the new columns).
  3. pnpm exec tsx server/scripts/import-internal-library-documents.ts
     with FRONTEND_REPO_ROOT pointing at the cabinet-frontend checkout, to put
     the committed PDF in the private bucket under the key the SQL row uses.

Frontend: cabinet-frontend pull request on cursor/library-internal-documents-a62c.

